{"step_index":552,"source":"MODEL","type":"GENERIC","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-21T22:34:21Z","content":"Created At: 2026-09-22T04:04:21+05:30\nCompleted At: 2026-09-22T04:04:21+05:30\nFile Path: `file:///C:/Users/k4ran/.gemini/antigravity/brain/e2c1cf9f-2dff-4bf4-a974-ef410441acfa/walkthrough.md`\nTotal Lines: 101\nTotal Bytes: 5765\nShowing lines 1 to 101\nThe following code has been modified to include a line number before every line, in the format: <line_number>: <original_line>. Please note that any changes targeting the original code should remove the line number, colon, and leading space.\n1: # 🛡️ SmartAGENT & Fluxnat Coder 3B — Walkthrough\n2: \n3: We have built the complete end-to-end **SmartAGENT Vulnerability Scanner** and the specialized **Fluxnat Coder 3B** fine-tuning & rebranding pipeline.\n4: \n5: ---\n6: \n7: ## 📦 What Was Built\n8: \n9: ### 1. The Fine-Tuning & Rebranding Suite (`fluxnat/Fluxnat-Coder-3B`)\n10: - [x] **[Fluxnat_Coder_3B_Training.ipynb](file:///c:/Users/k4ran/OneDrive/Desktop/smartAGENT/Fluxnat_Coder_3B_Training.ipynb)**: Complete 1-Click Google Colab training notebook powered by **Unsloth (2x faster, 70% less VRAM)** on a free **Tesla T4 GPU (16GB VRAM)**.\n11: - [x] **[prepare_datasets.py](file:///c:/Users/k4ran/OneDrive/Desktop/smartAGENT/prepare_datasets.py)**: Ingestion & formatting pipeline for CyberSecurity-1M, CTI, and local Chain-of-Thought reasoning datasets.\n12: - [x] **[data/custom_cot/security_cot.jsonl](file:///c:/Users/k4ran/OneDrive/Desktop/smartAGENT/data/custom_cot/security_cot.jsonl)**: Curated step-by-step reasoning samples teaching the model data flow tracking, CWE classification, and secure remediation.\n13: - [x] **[train.py](file:///c:/Users/k4ran/OneDrive/Desktop/smartAGENT/train.py)**: Fine-tuning script with QLoRA ($r=64$, $\\alpha=128$, targeting all linear projection layers). Supports both Unsloth and standard Hugging Face PEFT/TRL.\n14: - [x] **[rebrand.py](file:///c:/Users/k4ran/OneDrive/Desktop/smartAGENT/rebrand.py)**: Deep rebranding engine updating `config.json`, `tokenizer_config.json`, `generation_config.json`, and official Hugging Face Model Card.\n15: - [\n<truncated 2641 bytes>\n44: \n45: The notebook will:\n46: 1. Install Unsloth and load `huihui-ai/Qwen2.5-Coder-3B-Instruct-abliterated` in 4-bit (~2.5GB VRAM).\n47: 2. Train with QLoRA ($r=64$, $\\alpha=128$) on cybersecurity Chain-of-Thought reasoning data.\n48: 3. Merge adapters into a standalone 16-bit model.\n49: 4. Deeply rebrand every config and model card into **Fluxnat Coder 3B**.\n50: 5. Push the finished model directly to **`https://huggingface.co/fluxnat/Fluxnat-Coder-3B`**.\n51: \n52: ---\n53: \n54: ## 🔍 How to Run the Scanner\n55: \n56: You can run SmartAGENT directly from the command line:\n57: \n58: ### 1. View System Status\n59: ```bash\n60: python -m smartagent.cli info\n61: ```\n62: \n63: ### 2. Audit Any Codebase\n64: ```bash\n65: python -m smartagent.cli scan C:\\path\\to\\your\\project\n66: ```\n67: \n68: ### 3. Audit with AI Verification & Code Fix Generation\n69: Once your model is trained and available:\n70: ```bash\n71: python -m smartagent.cli scan C:\\path\\to\\your\\project --ai\n72: ```\n73: \n74: ### 4. Export JSON or Markdown Reports\n75: ```bash\n76: python -m smartagent.cli scan . --json audit_results.json --md audit_results.md\n77: ```\n78: \n79: ---\n80: \n81: ## ✅ Verification Results\n82: \n83: ### Unit Tests\n84: ```\n85: Running SmartAGENT unit tests...\n86:   [OK] test_secret_scanner_detects_aws_key passed\n87:   [OK] test_pattern_scanner_detects_sqli passed\n88:   [OK] test_pattern_scanner_detects_command_injection passed\n89:   [OK] test_pattern_scanner_clean_code_no_findings passed\n90:   [OK] test_config_scanner_dockerfile_root passed\n91:   [OK] test_security_scorer passed\n92: \n93: [ALL TESTS PASSED SUCCESSFULLY!]\n94: ```\n95: \n96: ### Dogfooding (SmartAGENT Scanning Itself)\n97: - Analyzed 22 project files.\n98: - Successfully caught hardcoded